;; world/rooms/wrongwater/x-3y7.room
(room
  region: wrongwater
  at: (-3 7)
  title: "The Inverted Fall"
  intent: "a column of water hangs from the roof like a waterfall stopped and turned over, and the only way to the nook above is up through it"
  bed: (air 0.15 water 0.3 hang 0.6 drone 0.6)
  light: 0.6
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "######        ###########"
   "######        ###########"
   "######~~######          #"
   "######~~#               #"
   "######~~#               #"
   "######~~#               #"
   "####                     "
   "####                     "
   "#########%  %############"
   "#########%  %############")
  things: ((mural at: (9 0) image: wrongwater))
  decor: auto)
;; The column (6-7, rows 3-6, 8 cells) is walled on both sides: col 5 hangs
;; from the roof and col 8 is the nook block's west face. Its bottom is two
;; rows over the floor (standing row 8), so a held jump enters it; swim up
;; and leap out at its top (row 3) into the air above (rows 1-2) and onto the
;; nook (8-13, standing row 2), where a mural shows Wrongwater itself: lakes
;; over dry ground. The nook is six rows over the floor and the only wall
;; under it is single, so the swim is the only way up. A hole (10-11) with
;; rough sides drops into Stepping Lakes and is the climb back from there.
;; East to Under the Well (rows 7-8).
